(GRM-19: primary ::= literal | identifier | func_call | "(" expr ")" - the
 first three alternatives hold (a literal, a bare identifier, and a call,
 all exercised elsewhere in this ledger). The fourth is FALSE - see
 Discrepancy 2 (cross-ref EXP-D5, expressions.md, which already found
 this: parentheses are Vox's comment delimiters, so `(x add y)` is a
 comment and "Print (x add y) multiply z." errors with "Expected a
 statement, got Multiply"). The real grouping punctuation is `{...}`
 (LANGUAGE.md:1853, 1859), which this production does not list as a
 `primary` alternative at all - so `primary` as literally written is
 both wrong (parens don't group) and incomplete (braces do, unlisted).
 This probe shows the working form.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox GRM-19.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   20
)
a number called x is 2.
a number called y is 3.
a number called z is 4.
Print {x add y} multiply z.
